# Terminal Dialogs

`dialog` provides small, modal terminal dialogs for application
using the Termina vocabulary. It is intended for information,
acknowledgement, and single-line input rather than menus or
full-screen editing.

DEPENDENCIES:

- termina
- rng

Before displaying a dialog, configure the terminal dimensions
with `dialog:configure` (rows followed by columns). The caller
is responsible for selecting an appropriate terminal input mode
and redrawing any application UI after a dialog is dismissed.

`dialog:show`, `dialog:error`, and `dialog:help` take a message
followed by a title. `dialog:read`, `dialog:password`, and
`dialog:prompt` take a prompt followed by a title and return the
entered line.

~~~
{{
  #0 'Width  var-n
  #0 'Height var-n
  #0 'Row    var-n
  #0 'Col    var-n

  #52 'DIALOG:WIDTH const

  :setup (:-)
    @Height #2 &n:div call #2 n:sub !Row
    @Width DIALOG:WIDTH n:sub #2 &n:div call !Col ;

  :bar (:-)
    $+ c:put DIALOG:WIDTH #2 n:sub [ $- c:put ] times $+ c:put ;

  :line (n-)
    @Row n:add @Col vt:row,col
    $| c:put DIALOG:WIDTH #2 n:sub &sp times $| c:put ;

  :draw (:-)
    setup
    fg:cyan @Row @Col vt:row,col bar
    #1 line #2 line #3 line
    @Row #4 n:add @Col vt:row,col bar
    vt:reset ;

  :title (s-)
    fg:red @Row #1 n:add @Col #2 n:add vt:row,col s:put ;

  :text (s-)
    fg:yellow @Row #2 n:add @Col #2 n:add vt:row,col
    DIALOG:WIDTH #4 n:sub s:left s:put ;
~~~

# Single-Line Input

`dialog:read` displays a normal, visible input line.
`dialog:password` returns the same input string, but displays
one or two randomly selected asterisks for each entered
character. Both readers accept CR or LF as the end of input, and
support backspace and delete.

~~~
  #0 'Password var-n
  #0 'MaskCount var-n
  #0 'MaskWidth var-n
  #0 'InputChar var-n
  'MaskWidths d:create #512 allot

  :done? (c-f)
    [ ASCII:CR eq? ] [ ASCII:LF eq? ] bi or ;

  :backspace? (c-cf)
    dup [ ASCII:BS eq? ] [ ASCII:DEL eq? ] bi or ;

  :erase-width (n-)
    [ #1 vt:left sp #1 vt:left ] times ;

  :erase (:-)
    buffer:size #2 gteq?
    [ @Password
      [ &MaskCount v:dec
        &MaskWidths @MaskCount a:fetch erase-width ]
      [ #1 erase-width ] choose ] if ;

  :mask-width (:-n)
    n:random #2 n:mod ;

  :mask (:-)
    mask-width #1 n:add !MaskWidth
    @MaskWidth &MaskWidths @MaskCount a:store
    &MaskCount v:inc
    @MaskWidth [ $* c:put ] times ;

  :echo (c-)
    !InputChar
    @InputChar backspace? nip
    &erase
    [ @InputChar done? [ ]
      [ @Password &mask [ @InputChar c:put ] choose ] choose ] choose ;

  :check-bs (c-)
    backspace? nip [ buffer:size #2 gteq?
      [ buffer:get drop ] if buffer:get drop ] if ;

  :input (ss-s)
    draw title text
    [ #0 !MaskCount s:empty buffer:set
      [ c:get !InputChar
        @InputChar buffer:add
        @InputChar echo
        @InputChar check-bs
        @InputChar done? ] until
      buffer:start s:chop ] buffer:preserve
    vt:reset ;

---reveal---
  :dialog:configure (:nn-)
    !Width !Height ;

  :dialog:show (:ss-)
    draw title text
    fg:cyan @Row #3 n:add @Col #2 n:add vt:row,col
    'Press_any_key s:put vt:reset c:get drop ;

  :dialog:error (:ss-) dialog:show ;
  :dialog:help  (:ss-) dialog:show ;

  :dialog:read (:ss-s)
    #0 !Password input ;

  :dialog:password (:ss-s)
    #-1 !Password input ;

  :dialog:prompt (:ss-s) dialog:read ;
}}
~~~
